     1	"""Starter kits (P7) — host-owned scaffolds the contracts/packs name.
     2	
     3	A contract declares ``artifact.starter_kit`` (app_shell / lead_form) and the prompt packs
     4	tell the model to "scaffold from the <name> starter" — but the names were bare strings
     5	with nothing behind them (a false affordance; the model hand-drew frames). A StarterKit
     6	resolves a name to a host-owned file scaffold (path → text), parameterized by the build's
     7	title, so the model EDITS a real frame instead of hand-drawing common chrome.
     8	
     9	Pure: AppSpec/render reuse from disco.core.appkit; no runtime/tool imports. The lead_form
    10	starter IS the AppKit default (single source — app_create scaffolds from it).
    11	"""
