   199	    """Return the ToolScope for an agent surface, narrowed by model_policy.
   200	
   201	    Contract #4: ONE exact keyword signature (not "policy or withheld_tools").
   202	    AGENT_TOOLS is the security allowlist (what is *callable*); the advertised
   203	    set shown to the LLM is narrowed by model_policy.withheld_tools.  Withheld
   204	    tools remain in allowed_tools so the engine repair loop and the planner-
   205	    safety backstop (readonly_tool_names) continue to key off the full
   206	    allowed set — they must never see a narrower boundary than the security one.
   207	
   208	    Tier / capability behaviour (driven entirely by the policy object):
   209	      • standard + anchored_edit=True  → advertised_tools=None (show all)
   210	      • standard + anchored_edit=False → file_str_replace withheld
   211	      • weak    + anchored_edit=True   → plan_step, update_plan_progress withheld
   212	      • weak    + anchored_edit=False  → all three withheld
   213	    """
   214	    withheld = model_policy.withheld_tools
   215	    if not withheld:
   216	        # Standard no-op: show the complete toolset (advertised_tools=None = all allowed).
   217	        return ToolScope(allowed_tools=AGENT_TOOLS, preset="agent")
   218	    return ToolScope(
   219	        allowed_tools=AGENT_TOOLS,
   220	        advertised_tools=AGENT_TOOLS - withheld,
   221	        preset="agent",
   222	    )

